From f93aca5adef8dd96f392eab27aa718ffa3d97649 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:16:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: add the reset line of the rk3399
 watchdog

WDT0 at 0xff848000 is reset by presetn_wdt0, bit 5 of
CRU_SOFTRST_CON20 (RK3399 TRM V1.4 Part 1, WDT and CRU chapters),
exported as SRST_P_WDT0 in dt-bindings/clock/rk3399-cru.h.

Without a reset line dw_wdt_stop() only marks the watchdog as running
and the hardware keeps counting through system sleep. On a Kobol
Helios64 and a ROCK Pi 4A, s2idle longer than the watchdog timeout ends
in a watchdog reset; CRU_GLB_RST_ST reads 0x10 afterwards, flagging a
watchdog reset. With the reset line dw_wdt_stop() can stop the watchdog,
and with "watchdog: dw_wdt: manage reset line during system
suspend/resume" the driver holds it in reset while the system sleeps.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5.1
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-base.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-base.dtsi
index 49c68fe65de6..1aa278ae8dc7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-base.dtsi
@@ -1748,6 +1748,7 @@ watchdog@ff848000 {
 		reg = <0x0 0xff848000 0x0 0x100>;
 		clocks = <&cru PCLK_WDT>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 120 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+		resets = <&cru SRST_P_WDT0>;
 	};
 
 	rktimer: rktimer@ff850000 {
